  "readOnlyHint": true
 },
 "description": "Reads code you have ALREADY migrated and reports Signal Forms traps that COMPILE and are still wrong \u2014 a missed signal call in a position TypeScript does not check, a deprecated-but-valid v21 rule shape, a pre-release API name, an AbstractControl left in a form() model, Reactive Forms imports left behind. Run it after tsc, not instead of it: anything the compiler already reports is deliberately not repeated here. Read-only. It proves the ABSENCE OF KNOWN DEFECTS, never correctness.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
